{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113104","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113104/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113104/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113104/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113104","id":3658750850,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc7aFBuC","number":113104,"title":"Custom light() function shaders does not accumulate specular and diffuse for multiple lights","user":{"login":"CookieBadger","id":53947784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTQ3Nzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53947784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger","html_url":"https://github.com/CookieBadger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-11-24T12:50:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T12:55:28Z","closed_at":"2025-11-24T12:51:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.6.dev\n\n### System information\n\nRTX3070 Vulkan - ForwardClustered\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a custom light shader like this:\n\n```glsl\nshader_type spatial;\n\nvoid light() {\n\tDIFFUSE_LIGHT = ATTENUATION * LIGHT_COLOR;\n}\n```\n\nwe see that the light which is processed last just overrides all previous lighting information, which makes little sense, in my opinion.\n\n<img width=\"909\" height=\"771\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ebded10f-5b78-467f-af53-716ec0324bb9\" />\n\nThis is because in scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl in the light_process() function, the values are just assigned (`=`) instead of added (`+=`):\n```glsl\n...\n#CODE : LIGHT\n\n\talpha = half(alpha_highp);\n\tdiffuse_light = hvec3(diffuse_light_highp); // should probably be += \n\tspecular_light = hvec3(specular_light_highp); // should probably be += \n```\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nuser shader sample above and add two lights with different colors. observe that they don't mix.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[customlightshader.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23723204/customlightshader.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"CookieBadger","id":53947784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTQ3Nzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53947784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger","html_url":"https://github.com/CookieBadger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/gists{/gist_id}"